{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779565617,"nonce":"Br5MMS9epLJKxAH8Rd7IvjjxX5s=","message":"Implementation status on branch feature/graph-templates:\\n\\nCompleted in this branch:\\n- Added `feedbax.graph_templates` as the built-in template/spec-factory module. It provides canonical factories for standard Network internals, top-level legacy-compatible Network specs, and Simple Feedback loop specs.\\n- Changed `spec_to_graph(Network)` to instantiate and execute the serialized Network subgraph as a `Graph` instead of lowering to `SimpleStagedNetwork`. Generic nodes with persisted subgraphs are also instantiated through the subgraph path.\\n- Added state-backed GRU/LSTM leaf components plus runtime recurrent initializer support, so Network subgraphs execute from leaf components with recurrent carries rather than hidden hard-coded composite state. LSTM wrapper now matches the current Equinox call contract.\\n- Added a graph-template Simple Feedback loop that executes as a normal GraphSpec/Graph path, including flattened mechanics feedback, Channel/efferent path, and nested Network graph execution.\\n- Updated the worker controller bridge so authored `Network` specs use `spec_to_graph(GraphSpec)` and `Graph.step()`; legacy `SimpleStagedNetwork` remains an explicit compatibility bridge and rejects LSTM instead of pretending the GRU-only fast path supports it.\\n- Added typed retained-observable/retention schema surfaces and Studio selector targets for ports, graph outputs, edges, recurrent carries, retained observables, task data, and state paths. This is the retained-observables rescope; full loss/artifact retention lowering remains follow-on work.\\n- Exposed executable built-in templates through the component registry and Studio Templates tab. Template nodes now persist their subgraphs in `graph.subgraphs`, not only a preview param.\\n- Preserved old imports/checkpoints at the compatibility boundary: `SimpleStagedNetwork` and `SimpleFeedback` classes remain importable; GraphSpec/Studio paths now prefer templates and explicit subgraph execution. No blind .eqx compatibility promise is added.\\n\\nTemplates currently in the built-in catalog:\\n- `feedbax.templates.network` / `Network Template` / executable / leaf graph: `input_mux -\u003e GRU|LSTM cell -\u003e readout` with recurrent hidden/cell carries.\\n- `feedbax.templates.simple_feedback` / `Simple Feedback Loop` / executable / feedback channel + Ravel + nested Network + efferent Channel + mechanics (+ optional force filter).\\n- Existing CDE registry templates are now marked display-only: `feedbax.templates.cde_standard`, `feedbax.templates.cde_decay`, `feedbax.templates.cde_anti_nf`, `feedbax.templates.cde_hybrid_v9b`.\\n\\nFollow-up issues created/updated:\\n- 4f835cb tracks Studio exposure of built-in templates as subgraph components; this branch implements the backend registry fields plus the frontend Templates tab.\\n- a1036a6 tracks deriving Channel/DelayLine/filter input prototypes instead of relying on hand-authored `input_shape`. This branch keeps `Channel.input_shape` documented/round-tripped because delayed scan state still needs concrete shapes.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- `uv run pytest tests/test_provider_contract.py tests/test_studio_workspace.py tests/test_graph.py tests/test_graph_templates.py` -\u003e 70 passed.\\n- `npm run build` in `web/` -\u003e passed.\\n- Additional smoke: registry templates instantiate and execute via `spec_to_graph`; Simple Feedback template executes over a short PointMass rollout.\\n\\nKnown residuals intentionally not collapsed into this branch:\\n- Full objective/loss lowering to retained observables and artifact retention is not complete here; the typed contract and selector enumeration are in place.\\n- Generic mechanics/plant worker execution is still a constrained bridge; authored Network controller execution is now graph-based, but full plant/loss generalization is a larger worker/runtime slice.\\n- RLRMP checkpoint migration remains in RLRMP b41c940.","files":null}]}